[00:15.56]Who is your friend, O God?
[00:19.96]Who in your tent may dwell?
[00:24.79]Who gains your friendship? Who gains your trust?
[00:29.78]Who really knows you well?
[00:34.72]All who embrace your Word,
[00:39.52]All who have faith in you,
[00:44.44]All who are loyal, all who are just,
[00:49.30]Living the truth for you.
[01:01.52]Who is your friend, O God?
[01:12.53]Who may approach your throne?
[01:16.50]Who brings delight and makes you rejoice?
[01:23.54]Whose name to you is known?
[01:28.36]All who exalt your name,
[01:31.18]All who your Word obey,
[01:36.23]All who are faithful, honest in heart,
[01:42.87]Truthful in all they say.
[01:50.36]Throwing our cares on you,
[01:53.72]Baring our hearts in prayer,
[02:00.15]Drawing us closer, bonding in love,
[02:05.10]Feeling your daily care,
[02:09.90]We yearn to be your friend.
[02:14.70]Long may our friendship grow.
[02:19.56]No greater Friend could we ever gain,
[02:24.46]No greater Friend we’ll know.
